{"en":"<h2>Hamaj regency (Funj sultanate)</h2><p class=\"meta\">1762 CE – 1821 CE · Sudan – Middle Nile</p><p class=\"hwks\"><b>How we know:</b> <span><bdi>2</bdi> sources</span><span class=\"hwkk\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"hwkt\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-describedby=\"hwkd-en\">Evidence kinds (derived)</button><span class=\"hwtip\" role=\"tooltip\" id=\"hwkd-en\">from the data types present</span>:</span><span>written sources</span><span class=\"hwkv\" hidden></span></p><p class=\"chp\">Part of: <a href=\"/?era=funj-sultanate-of-sennar\">Funj Sultanate of Sennar</a></p><details open><summary>Key events</summary><ul><li>Funj withdraw from Kordofan; Darfur turns east <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.189\">source</a></small></li><li>Abu Likaylik deposes Badi IV: the Hamaj regency begins <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.185\">source</a></small></li><li>Shendi supplants Sennar as the caravan market <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.183\">source</a></small></li><li>Death of Abu Likaylik and fifty years of civil war <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.185\">source</a></small></li><li>Shilluk raid destroys the settlement at the Nile confluence <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.197\">source</a></small></li><li>Jieng (Dinka) migration across the Sobat <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.197\">source</a></small></li><li>Mamluks fleeing Muhammad Ali settle at Dongola <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.185\">source</a></small></li><li>The enfeebled sultanate cannot resist the Turco-Egyptian advance <small class=\"kcites\"><a class=\"kcite\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · p.185\">source</a></small></li></ul></details><p class=\"srcs\"><small>Sources: <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a class=\"kcite\" data-rid=\"GHA5_CH7\" href=\"https://unesdoc.unesco.org/ark:/48223/pf0000184290\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot · 1992 · The Sudan, 1500–1800, ch.7 (General History of Africa V)\">Y.F. Hasan and B.A. Ogot 1992</a> pp.183, 185, 189, 197</span></small></p>","ar":"<h2>وصاية الهمج (سلطنة الفونج) <span class=\"vchip\" lang=\"ar\" aria-label=\"هذه المعلومة تحتاج إلى تحقق\">يحتاج تحقق</span></h2><p class=\"meta\">1762 م – 1821 م · السودان – النيل الأوسط</p><p class=\"hwks\"><b>كيف نعرف:</b> <span><bdi>2</bdi> مصادر</span><span class=\"hwkk\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"hwkt\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-describedby=\"hwkd-ar\">أنواع الأدلة (مستنتجة)</button><span class=\"hwtip\" role=\"tooltip\" id=\"hwkd-ar\">من أنواع البيانات الموجودة</span>:</span><span>مصادر مكتوبة</span><span class=\"hwkv\"><span class=\"vchip\">يحتاج تحقق</span> <bdi>9</bdi></span></p><p class=\"chp\">جزء من: <a href=\"/ar/?era=funj-sultanate-of-sennar\">سلطنة الفونج (سنار)</a></p><details open><summary>أحداث رئيسية</summary><ul><li>انسحاب الفونج من كردفان وتوجه دارفور شرقًا <span class=\"vchip\" lang=\"ar\" a